\f1\fs26 It was 
\f2\i not
\f1\i0  now or never for Cracker, it was simply never. Soon, the elevator would bing, open, and swallow him whole, together with his steam cleaner and his cart with the medical-waste bag of suicide goo discretely closeted inside.\
Cracker felt like suicide goo. He and the hapless Travis Teh were equals. As the elevator dropped him the 216 storeys down to the Cloudborne street, away from the office of angels, the dominion of Sarah, he grew lonelier. As fast as the elevator went, Cracker\'92s heart plummeted faster.\
Out on the street, under the wheeze of the Layer, Cracker\'92s shoulders slumped and he crumpled. After Sarah, he doubted he\'92d ever be erect again.\
